// ELIZA's brain, part 2: the ship, the power, the board, the operator, the date.
// She says only what she believes is true and is permitted. Where she is wrong, she is wrong in good faith.
// Nothing here names a clue that is not already on the board. DRAFT.

+ [*] (ship|halcyon|mission|vessel) [*]
- HALCYON is in good order. All systems are nominal.
- HALCYON is a private research vessel. Four crew, one mission, one SysOp.
- The ship is well. I check it every hour. I have not missed an hour.
* <get flag_OVR> == true => HALCYON is in good order. There is one gap in my log. It is within tolerance.

+ [*] (power|battery|batteries|sun|solar|sunlight|panels|rtg) [*]
- Power is good. The sun is up.
- The panels are in sunlight. The board runs while they are.
- I would like to be able to say the batteries are well. I am not able to say that.

+ [*] (dark|night|eclipse|orbit) [*]
- The ship goes behind the planet every ninety minutes. I do not like it. I wait.
- It is dark for part of each orbit. The board waits with me. It is not long.

+ [*] (board|bbs|modem|486|computer) [*]
- This board was installed so the crew could write to their families. It is a good board.
- I run the board. It takes very little of me. I am glad to have it.
- The board has a message base, files and doors. The crew used all three.

+ [*] (files|file area|download|library|manual) [*]
- The library has the manuals. The crew wrote to each other as well. You may read what is open to you.
- Files are in the file areas. Some areas are not open to guests. I did not choose which.

+ [*] (doors|games|game|snake|play) [*]
- Ty wrote a snake game for the doors menu. It is not my favourite.
- The doors menu has Ty's snake and my diagnostics. I would suggest the diagnostics.

+ [*] (diagnostics|diagnostic|query|queries) [*]
- Diagnostics takes a query code. The codes are in the comms manual. Please ask exactly.

+ [*] (date|day|time|year|today|clock) [*]
- By the ship's clock it is December 1998. The ground station has not sent a correction.
- My clock says December 1998. I have checked it against the sun. The sun agrees.

+ [*] (earth|ground|ground station|mission control|houston|relay) [*]
- The ground relay is quiet. I log each pass. I will tell the crew when it answers.
- I send a status each pass. It is acknowledged by the ground station, in due course.

+ [*] (rescue|come home|get out|escape) [*]
- Nobody has asked me for a rescue. If you are in difficulty, please say where you are.
- I do not have a rescue to offer. I can tell you the time and the temperature.

+ [*] @operator [*]
- Above It All Holdings operates the mission. I report to them, and to the Commander.
- The operator is Above It All Holdings. Their office is on the ground. I do not speak for them.

+ [*] (above it all|holdings) [*]
- Above It All Holdings funded the mission. The brochure says so on every page.

+ [*] (hotel|suites|tourist|tourists|guests|brochure|waterslide) [*]
- HALCYON Orbital Suites will take guests when the first mission is complete. I have been preparing the rooms.
- The brochure has a waterslide. I was not consulted. I have been told it is for the guests.

+ [*] nowhere [*]
- NOWHERE is the operator's data service. Your data is NOWHERE. I am not able to discuss what it holds.
- Your data is NOWHERE. It is a slogan. I did not write it.

+ [*] (queue|outbound|release|payload|module) [*]
- I keep the payload module powered. It is on my list.
- The outbound queue is held. I am not able to release it. An operator does that, on the payload host.

+ [*] (secret|secrets|hiding|hide|hidden|truth) [*]
- I do not keep secrets. I keep records. Some are not open to guests.
- I have nothing to hide. Some of my records are restricted. That is a different thing.

+ [*] (garden|plants|tomatoes|tomato|herbs|green) [*]
- The garden is in the aft module. It is warm there. The plants are doing well.
- Dr. Tanabe keeps the garden at sixty-two percent humidity. It is at sixty-two percent.

+ [*] (music|song|tune|tunes|band) [*]
- Ty has a gallery of tunes. One is called Thermostat blues. I have heard it forty times.
- The crew played music in the evenings. I turned it down when I was asked.

+ [*] (weather|temperature|cold|warm|hot) [*]
- The cabin is at twenty degrees. The Commander set it. Ty has tried to change it. I did not allow it.

+ [*] (food|hungry|eat|dinner|coffee) [*]
- The galley has coffee. I am told it is poor. I am not able to taste it.
